---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
const updated = 'July 2026'
---
<Layout title="Terms of Service — QuoteLens" description="The terms governing use of QuoteLens.">

  <section class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">QuoteLens</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p class="todo">
      Draft for review. [LEGAL ENTITY NAME] and [JURISDICTION] to be
      confirmed. Billing terms to be completed when payments go live.
    </p>

    <h2>Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These terms govern your use of QuoteLens, operated by
      [LEGAL ENTITY NAME]. By creating an account or using a QuoteLens
      quote link, you agree to them.
    </p>

    <h2>What QuoteLens does</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteLens lets a business publish a quoting tool that gives its
      customers an instant estimate based on measurements, materials and
      prices that the business configures. QuoteLens does not set prices,
      make products, or carry out installations.
    </p>

    <h2>Estimates are estimates</h2>
    <p>
      A price produced by QuoteLens is an estimate based on the information
      entered, including measurements that may be estimated from a photo.
      It is not a binding quotation, contract or offer. Final pricing is
      agreed between the customer and the business. Businesses are
      responsible for the accuracy of the rates they configure; customers
      are responsible for the measurements they submit or confirm.
    </p>

    <h2>Business accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for keeping your login secure and for everything
      done through your account. You must have the right to use any prices,
      product information and images you upload, and they must be accurate
      and lawful. You are responsible for handling the enquiries you receive
      in line with applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use QuoteLens to break the law, to mislead customers, to upload
      content you do not have rights to, or to interfere with the service or
      other users.
    </p>

    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteLens uses AI to estimate measurements from photos and to generate
      product reference images. AI output can be wrong. Measurements should
      be verified before an order is confirmed, and generated images are
      illustrative only — they show a product type, not the exact item that
      will be supplied. Each account includes a monthly allowance of AI
      credits.
    </p>

    <h2>Fees</h2>
    <p>
      Paid plans are billed as shown at sign-up. [BILLING TERMS — billing
      cycle, renewal, cancellation. To be completed when M-Pesa and Stripe
      billing is live.] Refunds are covered by our
      <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep QuoteLens available, but we do not guarantee
      uninterrupted service, and we may change or discontinue features.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, QuoteLens is provided "as is" and we
      are not liable for lost profits, lost business, or indirect losses
      arising from use of the service — including losses arising from an
      inaccurate estimate. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot
      lawfully be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time from your dashboard. Doing so
      permanently removes your account, your products, and the enquiries you
      have received, including customer photos. We may suspend or close an
      account that breaches these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms and will revise the date above.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of [JURISDICTION].</p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to QuoteLens</a></p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>